## SDK setup (both flows)

Load all three from the same version:

```html
<script src="https://js.braintreegateway.com/web/3.142.0-beta-editfi.1/js/client.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://js.braintreegateway.com/web/3.142.0-beta-editfi.1/js/paypalcheckout.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://js.braintreegateway.com/web/3.142.0-beta-editfi.1/js/datacollector.min.js"></script>
```

| Component | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `client.min.js` | Core client — `braintree.client.create()` |
| `paypalcheckout.min.js` | PayPal flows — `paypalCheckout.create()`, `createPayment()`, `loadPayPalSDK()`, `tokenizePayment()` |
| `datacollector.min.js` | Device data for risk/fraud signals on the sale |

> Note: the guide lists `datacollector.min.js` in setup but never wires it into a flow. If we
> want device data on the sale, add `braintree.dataCollector.create()` and pass `deviceData`
> into `transaction.sale`. Not implemented by default — decide explicitly before adding.

**Shared boot sequence** (identical in both flows through `loadPayPalSDK`; only the token
source and the final render call differ):

```js
const clientInstance = await braintree.client.create({ authorization: clientToken });
const paypalCheckout = await braintree.paypalCheckout.create({
  client: clientInstance,
  autoSetDataUserIdToken: true, // reads the identity token from the client token onto the SDK load
});
await paypalCheckout.loadPayPalSDK({
  vault: true,
  currency: 'USD',
  intent: 'capture',
  components: 'buttons,messages,saved-payment-methods',
  env: 'sandbox', // REQUIRED in sandbox
});
```

